Pending direct PUT can resurrect deleted objects
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/042318b2fbf48191a6edbe6d7410d83c?repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin&sev=
Criticality: medium (attack path: medium)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
This finding was valid for commit `2f977e8`. The current branch fixed the
reported delete path in `1a4ff75e2005d7e9088c1b73f732c940f43704cd` by routing
object deletes and delete-marker insertion through the object metadata command
stream, so they drain any pending command for the bucket before reading or
mutating current object state.

The pinned local regression is
`object_delete_drains_pending_direct_put_commit_before_delete`: a partial
direct PUT commit leaves a pending command, current-object delete first applies
that command and deletes the new generation, and a later reservation does not
resurrect the deleted object.

